# Workspace Settings

Configure your workspace to match your organization's needs and branding.

## Accessing Settings

1. Click **Settings** in the sidebar
2. Select the settings category you want to configure

## General Settings

Found under **Settings > General**.

### Workspace Name

The display name for your workspace. This appears in:
- The sidebar header
- Member invitations
- Email communications

### Workspace Slug

The URL-friendly identifier for your workspace (e.g., `my-company`). This appears in all workspace URLs:

```
https://app.example.com/en/my-company/events
```

**Note:** Changing the slug will update all workspace URLs. Share new links with your team after changing.

## Branding

Found under **Settings > Branding**.

Customize the visual appearance of your workspace.

### Logo

Upload your organization's logo. The logo appears in:
- The sidebar header
- Email templates (when configured)
- Public-facing pages

**Tip:** Upload both light and dark mode versions for the best appearance across themes.

### Colors

Set your brand colors:

- **Primary Color** - Main brand color for buttons and accents
- **Accent Color** - Secondary color for highlights

Colors can be set separately for light and dark modes.

## Email Settings

Found under **Settings > Email**.

Configure default email sender information for your workspace.

### From Name

The name that appears as the sender in emails. For example:
- "Events Team"
- "Your Company Events"

### From Email

The email address used as the sender. This should be a valid email address that your team monitors.

**Note:** These are default values. Individual events can override these settings.

## Members

Found under **Settings > Members**.

Manage who has access to your workspace. See the [Inviting Members](/docs/admin-guide/inviting-members) documentation for details.

## Danger Zone

Found at the bottom of **Settings > General**.

### Delete Workspace

**Warning:** This action is permanent and cannot be undone.

Deleting a workspace will remove:
- All events
- All guest records
- All email templates
- All RSVP data
- All member associations

Only the workspace **Owner** can delete the workspace.

### Before Deleting

1. Export any data you need to keep
2. Inform all workspace members
3. Consider transferring ownership if someone else should maintain the data

## Settings by Role

Not all settings are available to all roles:

| Setting | Owner | Admin | Manager | Member |
|---------|-------|-------|---------|--------|
| General (name, slug) | Yes | No | No | No |
| Branding | Yes | No | No | No |
| Email defaults | Yes | No | No | No |
| Members | Yes | Yes | No | No |
| Delete workspace | Yes | No | No | No |
